LeetCode: Minimum Moves to Equal Array Elements III
Problem: Minimum Moves to Equal Array Elements III
Approach: Greedy
Intuition
The goal is to make all elements of the array equal using the minimum number of moves.

In this problem, one move allows us to increase or decrease an element by 1.

To minimize the total number of moves, we can make every element equal to the maximum element in the array.
- Find the maximum element using max_element().
- Calculate the difference between the maximum element and every other element.
- Add all differences to get the minimum number of moves.
C++ Code
class Solution {
public:
    int minMoves(vector<int>& nums) {
        int maxi = *max_element(begin(nums), end(nums));

        int count = 0;

        for (const int& num : nums) {
            count += (maxi - num);
        }

        return count;
    }
};


Complexity Analysis
- Time Complexity: \(O(n)\)
  - Finding the maximum element takes \(O(n)\).
  - Traversing the array to calculate the total moves takes \(O(n)\).
- Space Complexity: \(O(1)\)
  - Only a few extra variables are used.
